{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And it shall be.</b> Now they thought that the word of HaShem was not fundamental, but only a pain in the hand, to train them lest they go to Egypt, as it is written, \"Woe to those who go down to Egypt for help\" (Isaiah 31:1), for it is one pericope."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:34.895290978Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}